WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.900
Coding Exercise 4 practices a safe UPDATE using a
stable key Your

00:00:04.925 --> 00:00:08.262
task is to update the patient with MRN one zero zero
six

00:00:08.288 --> 00:00:12.525
so the age becomes twenty-eight Then use RETURNING
to show the MRN

00:00:12.738 --> 00:00:18.012
name and age The starter code already has UPDATE
patients SET WHERE

00:00:18.175 --> 00:00:22.238
and RETURNING You need to complete the SET
expression and the WHERE

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:28.312
condition SET describes what value changes Write age
equals twenty-eight

00:00:29.188 --> 00:00:33.950
WHERE describes which row can change Use MRN equals
the quoted value

00:00:33.962 --> 00:00:38.812
MRN one zero zero six Before running the update
pause and ask

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:42.700
how many rows you expect to affect The answer should
be one

00:00:42.712 --> 00:00:46.775
because the MRN is a stable unique identifier in
this practice database

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:51.762
Click Run and Check and inspect the returned row The
MRN and

00:00:51.788 --> 00:00:54.838
name should identify the same patient and the age
should now be

00:00:54.850 --> 00:01:01.112
twenty-eight This exercise is short but the safety
idea is important Never

00:01:01.138 --> 00:01:04.963
think of UPDATE as only SET a new value A safe
UPDATE

00:01:04.988 --> 00:01:09.850
also requires a precise target In real database work
the WHERE clause

00:01:09.862 --> 00:01:12.475
is often the most important part of an UPDATE
statement
